vices to the offshore oil and gas exploration and production industry. It also provides vessel management services, marine transportation, logistics support, subsea construction, inspection, repair and maintenance, trenching and burial services, subsea well intervention services, defense support services, and integrated marine solutions for the oilfield, renewables, defense, aerospace, telecommunications, and disaster response markets. The company was formerly known as Hornbeck-Leevac Marine Services, Inc. and changed its name to Hornbeck Offshore Services, Inc. in May 2002. Hornbeck Offshore Services, Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is based in Covington, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Todd M. Hornbeck | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $936,671 (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Hornbeck Offshore Services, Inc is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.7B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.44\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 15% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 36% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hornbeck Offshore Services Inc (HOS) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Helix Merger Fuels $1. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/hornbeck-offshore-services-inc-hos-011048272.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793927448.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earn